# 00_Modelfile
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Turn your quantized GGUF artifact from Chapter 14 into a first-class Ollama
# model. Build it with:
#
#     ollama create medical-gemma -f 00_Modelfile
#     ollama run medical-gemma "What are the first-line treatments for T2DM?"
#
# The three things that make this a REAL deployment rather than a raw file:
#   1. FROM points at the exact GGUF you shipped, so the model you serve is
#      byte-for-byte the one you evaluated.
#   2. TEMPLATE bakes in the Gemma 4 chat format, so callers send plain
#      messages and never have to hand-assemble <|turn> / <turn|> tokens.
#   3. PARAMETER pins the decode settings you validated, so behaviour is the
#      same on every machine that pulls this model.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

FROM ./medical-gemma-Q4_K_M.gguf

# Gemma 4 chat template. The model was fine-tuned against this exact format;
# a mismatched template is the classic cause of a model that "loads fine but
# answers weirdly" (see Chapter 14's pitfalls).
#
# What changed from Gemma 2/3:
#   - Turns are wrapped in <|turn>ROLE ... <turn|> instead of
#     <start_of_turn>ROLE ... <end_of_turn>.
#   - There is a real "system" role, so the SYSTEM prompt below gets its own
#     turn instead of being folded into the first user message.
#   - Gemma 4 has a thinking mode, switched on by putting <|think|> in the
#     system turn. Chapter 14 trained with enable_thinking=False, so this
#     template never emits <|think|>. That keeps serving identical to training.
#
# The BOS token is not written here; Ollama adds it from the GGUF metadata.
# This template covers plain chat only (no tool calling or images), which is
# all the medical QA model was trained on.
TEMPLATE """{{- if .System }}<|turn>system
{{ .System }}<turn|>
{{ end }}
{{- range .Messages }}
{{- if eq .Role "user" }}<|turn>user
{{ .Content }}<turn|>
{{ else if eq .Role "assistant" }}<|turn>model
{{ .Content }}<turn|>
{{ end }}
{{- end }}<|turn>model
"""

# Pin decode settings you validated during evaluation. Low temperature for a
# domain where you want consistent, defensible answers. (Google's general
# defaults for Gemma 4 are temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 64; we override
# them on purpose.)
PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER top_k 40
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER stop "<turn|>"

# Bake the guardrail persona into the served model so every caller inherits it,
# not just the ones who remember to send a system prompt. A system message
# sent by the caller replaces this default.
SYSTEM """You are a medical question-answering assistant for clinicians.
Answer concisely and cite the class of evidence when relevant.
You are not a substitute for professional judgement; flag when a question
needs a specialist or more patient context."""
